        "hypothesis": "A stable byte-radix sort with independent per-thread histograms and deterministic disjoint scatters will replace comparison-heavy recursive partitioning for large arrays and reduce elapsed time on four ARM64 cores.",
        "id": "7678ef3a06ba4cc9",
        "ordinal": 1,
        "parent_id": null,
        "role": "B",
        "source_commits": [],
        "sources": [],
        "transformations": {
          "files": [
            "src/quicksort.c"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Add an OpenMP-gated four-pass signed integer radix sort for large arrays; histogram counting and scatter writes are partitioned so no loop-carried write dependency is asserted as SIMD-safe.",
            "Turn the post-sort read-only adjacent comparison into a legal SIMD bitwise-OR reduction while preserving its return value."
          ]
        },
